# Git Commit & Push — Branch Alignment (Mandatory)

Every `git commit` and `git push` must land on a **task branch whose name matches what is in the commit**. Do not reuse whatever branch happens to be checked out.

## Wrong vs right

| Wrong | Why |
|---|---|
| Commit note-delete fix on `fix/activity-history-html-escape` | Branch topic ≠ diff topic; PR/review/history become misleading |
| Clip delete fix on `feature/extension-safety-expiry-icons` | Unrelated open feature branch; fix must be `fix/clips-delete-resurrection` from `main` |
| One branch named `ui` for weeks of mixed work | Cannot review, revert, or ship one change safely |
| Push to `main` without explicit user approval | Breaks stable default branch policy |

| Right | Example |
|---|---|
| Bug fix branch for bug fix work | `fix/notes-delete-persistence`, `fix/clips-delete-resurrection` |
| Refactor branch for refactor work | `refactor/popup-events-extraction` |
| Two focused branches when two unrelated ships | `fix/notes-delete` + `refactor/popup-event-listeners` |

## Before staging (agent checklist)

1. Run `git branch --show-current` and `git status --short`.
2. **Name the work** in 1–2 short phrases from the actual diff (not the old branch name).
3. **Compare** current branch to that name:
   - If it matches → proceed.
   - If it does not match → **stop**; do not commit on the wrong branch.
4. Decide **one branch or two**:
   - **One branch** — single user-visible outcome or one refactor slice (preferred).
   - **Two branches** — two independent outcomes (e.g. `fix/…` + `refactor/…`) that can merge separately; split via cherry-pick or separate commits, not one mixed commit.

## Creating or switching branches

From latest `main` (or agreed base):

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git checkout -b fix/notes-delete-persistence   # example
```

If work already exists on the wrong branch:

- **Preferred:** cherry-pick the fix commit onto a new branch from `main`, then reset the wrong branch to remove the stray commit.
- Create the correct branch from current HEAD only if the wrong branch has no unrelated commits you need to drop: `git checkout -b fix/correct-topic`
- Recovery example (fix landed on wrong feature branch):

```bash
git stash push -m "wip"                    # if uncommitted work on wrong branch
git checkout main && git pull
git checkout -b fix/clips-delete-resurrection
git cherry-pick <fix-commit-sha>
git push -u origin fix/clips-delete-resurrection
git checkout feature/wrong-branch
git reset --hard <commit-before-fix>
git push --force-with-lease origin feature/wrong-branch
```

Tell the user when a branch mismatch is detected **before** committing.

## Commit & push sequence (every time)

1. Confirm branch aligns with diff (above).
2. Stage only files for this task (user said “commit all” → still exclude secrets and unrelated files).
3. Conventional commit message: `type: short description` (see `git-workflow.mdc`).
4. `git commit` → report SHA.
5. `git push -u origin HEAD` only on the **task** branch, never `main` unless user explicitly requests.

## Branch naming map (PasteCraft)

| Work in diff | Branch prefix | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Bug / regression | `fix/` | `fix/notes-delete-persistence`, `fix/clips-delete-resurrection` |
| New capability | `feat/` | `feat/activity-log-recover` |
| Structure move, no behavior change | `refactor/` | `refactor/popup-events-extraction` |
| Tests only | `test/` | `test/popup-events-smoke` |
| Docs / rules only | `docs/` | `docs/git-branch-alignment` |
| Tooling, deps, CI | `chore/` | `chore/npm-test-script` |

Use **kebab-case** after the prefix; 2–5 words; no dates in the name.

## When user says “git commit all”

1. Still run branch alignment check first.
2. If diff contains **two unrelated** areas (e.g. bug fix + large refactor), **ask** whether to split into two branches before one commit.
3. Draft commit message from the **diff**, not from the current branch name.
4. Push to `origin` on the aligned branch only.

## Agent must say out loud

Before commit:

> Branch: `<current>`. Work: `<summary>`. Aligned: yes/no. Action: `<commit here | create branch X | split into two branches>`.

This prevents repeats of committing popup/notes work on an activity-history branch.
